WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.714
You have seen 你好 written down. That writing has a name: hànzì. Now it's worth understanding what a hànzì is.

2
00:00:07.714 --> 00:00:17.429
A letter on its own means nothing — the T in tree doesn't mean tree. A hànzì is different: it usually carries a whole meaning by itself.

3
00:00:17.429 --> 00:00:25.714
Listen, and look at the shape: a trunk down the middle, branches opening to the sides. Many hànzì began as pictures.

4
00:00:25.714 --> 00:00:37.429
木 is the writing. mù is the sound. The falling mark is the tone. Tree is the meaning. None can be guessed from the others — that is why they always appear together.

5
00:00:37.429 --> 00:00:39.629
This is not scored.

6
00:00:39.629 --> 00:00:48.557
Now that you know what a hànzì is, it's worth practising the shapes — because shape is what tells one character from another.
